WSL training data (~/sam2-training)
==================================

What this is
------------
A local-SSD copy of the NAS training versions, used by the trainer and the
annotation gallery containers (~/sam2-training is bind-mounted at /data-local).

  ~/sam2-training/
    v1b/ v2/ v3/ ...        one folder per version, flat layout:
      RC1/ RC2/ RPC1/ RPC2/   <VOL>/manifest.jsonl, annotation_crops.sqlite,
                              images/, masks/, approved.json, ignore.json, ignored/
    current -> v3           relative symlink; the containers read /data-local/current

Source of truth: Y:\SAM2TrainingData\TEM\<version>\<VOL> (the NAS, built with
version-bump / version-sync). SEM data is separate: Y:\SAM2TrainingData\SEM\<version>\<VOL>
(sem-version-*), mirrored to ~/sam2-training-sem with sem-sync_training_data.sh and
sem-select_training_data.sh (same arguments; set SAM2_TRAINING_DEST_SEM to move it). SEM never
touches ~/sam2-training or its `current` link. The container mounts one or the other, chosen by
`run-cursor-dev.ps1 -Modality TEM|SEM` (see TEM.env / SEM.env; README "Run / Dev Container"). WSL copies are plain ext4 (no reflinks), so every
version costs its full size.

Version names
-------------
A training SET is v<SET> or v<SET>.<REVISION>: v2, v2.1. v2.1 is a repopulated or
tweaked v2 made with the same creation rules; new creation rules mean a new number
(v3). Revisions order numerically (v2 < v2.1 < v2.10 < v3). A trailing letter (v1b)
is the old style: still accepted, do not create new ones. current is a pointer, not
a version. Models have their own numbers (v<VERSION>.<EPOCH>); see
.cursor/rules/naming-conventions.mdc.

What is copied
--------------
Only what training and the annotation gallery read: images/, masks/, manifest.jsonl, the catalog
and the *.json files, plus overlays/thumb and overlays/parts (the gallery serves those). Left out:
_work/ (the exporter's cache), the full-size overlay renders directly under overlays/ (tens of GB,
viewing only), and overlays/cardmask (rebuilt on demand). The list is SYNC_NEVER_COPY /
SYNC_OVERLAY_KEEP in training_data_common.sh. Folders already present in an older mirror are
left alone, not deleted; remove them by hand to reclaim the space. A folder deleted from the
source is no longer removed from the mirror.

Review state that must survive a mirror
---------------------------------------
Per volume: approved.json, ignore.json, ignored/ (rejected mask PNGs), and the
location_scores table in annotation_crops.sqlite. The NAS does not have these.
sync_training_data.sh keeps them (excluded from rsync --delete, scores saved and
merged back, rejected masks moved back to ignored/).

One-time setup
--------------
  # NAS share as a Linux path. drvfs often cannot mount a mapped Y:, so use CIFS.
  sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y cifs-utils
  sudo mkdir -p /mnt/y

  # Credentials (same user/password as the Docker storage4.cred), root-only
  sudo tee /root/.storage4.cred >/dev/null <<'EOF'
  username=jamesan
  password=YOUR_PASSWORD
  EOF
  sudo chmod 600 /root/.storage4.cred
  (remove the two leading spaces on the credential lines if you paste this)

  # Test by hand first (read-only: the mirror only reads)
  sudo mount -t cifs //192.168.0.199/Data /mnt/y -o credentials=/root/.storage4.cred,uid=$(id -u),gid=$(id -g),vers=3.1.1,ro,rsize=8388608,wsize=8388608,cache=loose,actimeo=20,nostrictsync,nobrl,noperm,mfsymlinks,iocharset=utf8
  ls /mnt/y/SAM2TrainingData/TEM

  # Then make it survive restarts (WSL runs `mount -a` at startup)
  sudo umount /mnt/y
  echo '//192.168.0.199/Data /mnt/y cifs credentials=/root/.storage4.cred,uid=1000,gid=1000,vers=3.1.1,ro,rsize=8388608,wsize=8388608,cache=loose,actimeo=20,nostrictsync,nobrl,noperm,mfsymlinks,iocharset=utf8,_netdev,nofail 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
  sudo mount -a && ls /mnt/y/SAM2TrainingData/TEM

  Notes: uid/gid 1000 must match `id -u` / `id -g`. Add multichannel,max_channels=4 for
  faster large copies. actimeo=20 means NAS-side changes can take ~20 s to show up, so
  wait after version-sync before mirroring. If vers=3.1.1 is refused, try 3.0.
  Errors: (2)/(113) host unreachable; (13) bad user or password.

  # Repo scripts (D: drive), strip CRLF that git on Windows may have added
  cd /mnt/d/src/git/Sam2Trainer
  sed -i 's/\r$//' scripts/WSL/*.sh
  chmod +x scripts/WSL/*.sh

  # Optional: call the scripts from anywhere. Use symlinks, not copies: the script follows the link back into
  # the repo to find training_data_common.sh and annotation_crops/scores.py, and a git pull then updates it.
  mkdir -p ~/bin
  ln -sf "$PWD/scripts/WSL/sync_training_data.sh" ~/bin/sync_training_data.sh
  ln -sf "$PWD/scripts/WSL/select_training_data.sh" ~/bin/select_training_data.sh
  ln -sf "$PWD/scripts/WSL/sem-sync_training_data.sh" ~/bin/sem-sync_training_data.sh
  ln -sf "$PWD/scripts/WSL/sem-select_training_data.sh" ~/bin/sem-select_training_data.sh
  rm -f ~/bin/training_data_common.sh          # a stale copy from before, if any
  # If the checkout is not at /mnt/d/src/git/Sam2Trainer, say where it is:
  export SAM2_TRAINER_REPO=/mnt/d/src/git/Sam2Trainer

  # Put these in ~/.bashrc to skip typing them
  export TRAINING_DATA_SRC=/mnt/y/SAM2TrainingData   # the scripts add /TEM or /SEM themselves
  export SAM2_TRAINING_DEST=$HOME/sam2-training

Run these in the WSL Ubuntu shell, not inside a container.

Back up the review state first (every time before a mirror)
-----------------------------------------------------------
  cd ~/sam2-training
  tar czf ~/review-backup-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M).tgz \
    $(find . -maxdepth 3 \( -name approved.json -o -name ignore.json -o -name ignored \
        -o -name annotation_crops.sqlite \) -not -path './current/*')

Mirror a NEW version (example: v3, carrying review state from v2)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  cd /mnt/d/src/git/Sam2Trainer
  scripts/WSL/sync_training_data.sh -n -clone-from v2 v3    # dry run, changes nothing
  scripts/WSL/sync_training_data.sh -clone-from v2 v3       # real run, then points current at v3

Hardlink caveat: files shared between versions are ONE file. rsync replaces a changed
file with a new one, so the older version keeps its content. But editing a file in place
inside a version (a text editor, a tool opening it for write) changes every version that
shares it. The catalog and review files are copied for real for this reason. Check the
saving with: du -sh ~/sam2-training/v2 ~/sam2-training/v3 (du counts shared files once
per run, so list both versions in one command).

Refresh an EXISTING version (example: v3 was re-exported on the NAS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  scripts/WSL/sync_training_data.sh -n v3
  scripts/WSL/sync_training_data.sh v3

Flags
-----
  -n               dry run: layout check, seeding, and rsync changes are listed
  -j N             parallel rsync jobs, one per volume and folder (default: CPUs, at most 8)
  -clone-from vX   build the new version as a hardlink clone of vX, then rsync only the
                   changes (unchanged files share disk space). The catalog and review
                   files are real copies. Implies -seed-from. The new version must not exist.
  -seed-from vX    copy approved.json / ignore.json / ignored/ and location_scores
                   from local version vX into volumes that lack them (never overwrites)
  -noselect        mirror but leave `current` alone
  -force-layout    allow a flat/nested mismatch (the destination takes the source layout)
  (no version)     mirror the highest version found at the source

What to check afterwards
------------------------
  readlink ~/sam2-training/current                 # expect v3
  ls ~/sam2-training/v3/RC1/manifest.jsonl         # flat: manifest is directly under the volume
  # Output lines per volume, compare with your backup:
  #   saved N location_scores row(s) for <VOL>
  #   restored location_scores for <VOL>: N row(s) now
  #   kept reject list <VOL>: N location(s), M mask(s) moved

If `current` changed, restart the gallery container so it re-reads the catalog:
  docker restart sam2-trainer-annotation-gallery-1

Problems
--------
  "refusing to mirror" / layout mismatch
      One side is flat, the other still has <VOL>/AnnotationCrops/. Flatten the NAS
      version with `version-flatten vN` there; locally, the destination is already
      flat. Use -force-layout only if you mean it.
  "missing source"
      The share is not mounted (NAS off or network not up at WSL start): sudo mount /mnt/y
  "$'\r': command not found" or bad interpreter
      CRLF line endings: sed -i 's/\r$//' scripts/WSL/*.sh
  Mirror failed partway
      The script prints where it kept the saved location_scores copy (a /tmp dir).
      Fix the cause and re-run; the same version can be mirrored again safely.
  Old nested folders (~/sam2-training/RC1 etc. at the top level)
      Not used by current versions. Leave them or delete once you are sure.
